  "kind": "recipe",
  "metadata": {
    "alignment": "unspecified",
    "description": "Still-deployable historical disk-offload Candidate using the exact official native LTX 1.3.0 two-stage pipeline, BF16 checkpoint, distilled refinement LoRA, spatial upscaler, and Gemma 3 companion closure. The 89 GB startup and 75 GB steady declarations conservatively apply only the pinned upstream's documented 31 GB disk-versus-CPU offload reduction, with 8 GB growth and 8 GB system reserve for a 97 GB admission total; physical Spark acceptance remains pending. LTX-2.5 BF16 is the current fidelity baseline and LTX-2.5 FP8-cast is the current lower-memory canary; this immutable execution contract remains available for reproducibility.",
    "tags": [
      "executable",
      "candidate",
      "build-unvalidated",
      "historical",
      "superseded",
      "disk-offload",
      "lightricks",
      "ltx",
      "video",
      "audio",
      "synchronized",
      "pytorch-pipeline",
      "single",
      "spark"
    ],
    "title": "LTX-2 19B dev BF16 native synchronized single Spark (superseded)"
  },
